<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Galilee</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Galilee is a region in the north of present-day Israel. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saladin">Saladin</a>'s victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crusader-states">Crusaders</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-hattin">Hattin</a> in 1187, near the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sea-of-galilee">Sea of Galilee</a>, was the foundation of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ayyubid-empire">Ayyubid Empire</a>'s reconquest, and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mamluk">Mamluk</a> victory over the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mongols">Mongols</a> at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-ain-jalut">Ain Jalut</a> in 1260 in Galilee set a lasting western frontier for the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ilkhanate">Ilkhanate</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/galilee.jpg" alt="Galilee" width="320" height="263" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Dolní_Galilea.svg: Daniel Baránek derivative work: TheCuriousGnome (talk) · CC BY 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Lower_Galilee_map.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
